<header><p class="enc-kicker">Religion / idea · deity</p><h1 class="enc-title">Neptune</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Neptune was the Roman god of fresh water and the sea, identified with the Greek <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/poseidon">Poseidon</a>. His festival, the Neptunalia, was held in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rome">Rome</a> on 23 July. Temples and dedications to him were made across the empire, especially by sailors and in port towns.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/neptune.jpg" alt="Neptune" width="320" height="320" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: NASA / Voyager 2 / PDS / OPUS / Ardenau4 · CC0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Neptune_Voyager2_color_calibrated.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
